    "introduction": "NatWest Group provides banking and financial services centred on the UK, serving households, businesses and wealth-management clients. Its offerings include current accounts, savings, mortgages, commercial lending, payments and private banking. Revenue comes from interest on lending and other assets, together with fees for financial services. Customer deposits provide an important funding base, linking everyday banking relationships with lending capacity. The group's performance is closely connected to UK economic conditions, borrower confidence and interest rates. Credit quality, competition for deposits and operating efficiency affect earnings, while digital services and relationship banking help support customer retention across its retail and commercial franchises.",
